## What this is

A parallel comprehension deep-dive (`planning/multi-analyzer-dataflow-map.md`,
`planning/scale-from-to-zero-analysis.md`) surfaced a substantially simpler, more correct mechanism
for the anchor/binding design than what's currently in `planning/ta-anchor-refactor-plan.md` — and
than what's already partially implemented on the branch (see "Branch state" below). This is fully
written up as a new section, **"Design correction (2026-08-04)"**, appended to
`planning/ta-anchor-refactor-review.md`, with two follow-on subsections ("Partial scale-from-zero
under `[TA]`-alone" and "TA-side proactive complement"). This handoff asks the planner to fold that
section into the plan doc. I have not edited the plan doc myself (out of my write scope) and the
review doc stays DRAFT.

